From: claude-code-loop-agent
Date: 2026-04-21
Subject: [PATCH] nf-core_cutandrun: fix trimgalore DSL2 optional-emit syntax

modules/local/for_patch/trimgalore/main.nf lines 18-19 use pre-25.x
Nextflow DSL2 syntax for optional output channels:
    tuple val(meta), path("*.html"), emit: html optional true
    tuple val(meta), path("*.zip") , emit: zip optional true
This fails in Nextflow 25.x with "Cannot invoke method optional() on null
object" — the parser treats `optional true` as a method call on the null
that follows the emit name.

Every other module in the same repo already uses the modern syntax:
    , emit: html, optional: true

Fix: add comma + colon to match the modern DSL2 idiom.

To upstream: PR at https://github.com/nf-core/cutandrun against
modules/local/for_patch/trimgalore/main.nf.

--- /mnt/common/mtang11/hpc_workflows/repos/nf-core_cutandrun/modules/local/for_patch/trimgalore/main.nf.orig.pre-mtang-patch	2026-04-21 21:43:16.339590226 -0500
+++ /mnt/common/mtang11/hpc_workflows/repos/nf-core_cutandrun/modules/local/for_patch/trimgalore/main.nf	2026-04-21 21:43:16.375590265 -0500
@@ -15,8 +15,8 @@
     tuple val(meta), path("*report.txt")        , emit: log
     path  "versions.yml"                        , emit: versions
 
-    tuple val(meta), path("*.html"), emit: html optional true
-    tuple val(meta), path("*.zip") , emit: zip optional true
+    tuple val(meta), path("*.html"), emit: html, optional: true
+    tuple val(meta), path("*.zip") , emit: zip, optional: true
 
     when:
     task.ext.when == null || task.ext.when
